+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+This specification defines how the registry treats tool input, how the result reaches a provider, and which failures remain exceptions.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required properties, wrong types and disallowed enum members before invoking an executor; its returned `ToolResponse.result` and log lines name the property path and constraint without revealing input values; an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: returns safe constraint errors before executing and still throws for an unknown tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21)).
+- Valid input reaches the executor unchanged, including unknown properties, without coercion or defaults; a static definition is compiled at registration and its validator is reused across calls ([validated by: passes accepted input and unknown keys unchanged while reusing a static schema across ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- Registration of a static tool with an uncompilable JSON Schema throws immediately and names the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema during registration and names its tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+- A function-valued definition resolves for each execution, and the input is checked against that call's resolved schema, with compiled validators cached by schema object ([validated by: validates each function-sourced definition against the schema returned for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L111)).
+- A validation rejection is a tool result available to the provider on its next round, so the model can correct the call within the existing tool-round budget without ending the conversation ([validated by: lets the model read a rejected call and correct it in the next tool round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L140)).
